From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:52:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] sane.ds, twain_32, twaindsm: the scanner's own window opens and scans; TWAINDSM.DLL, TWAIN 2's source manager, for 64-bit programs (9818)

Scanning from a TWAIN program with the scanner's own window -- what most
programs show, IrfanView's Acquire among them -- and from 64-bit programs:

- sane.ds's window (a property sheet built from the SANE options) read
  option values into one int or 255 bytes whatever the option's size (an
  int array such as a gamma table: 16 KB): the window came up empty,
  crashed (64-bit) or overflowed the stack (IrfanView's 32-bit TWAIN stub).
  Values are read into buffers of the option's size, the sheet header is
  zeroed and the page count bounded.
- 64-bit programs load TWAIN 2's data source manager, TWAINDSM.DLL, which
  Wine did not have: IrfanView 64-bit fell back to its 32-bit stub, other
  programs found no scanner. twaindsm.dll is built from twain_32's sources;
  both now speak TWAIN 2: DAT_ENTRYPOINT (the manager's DSM_Entry and memory
  functions), DAT_CALLBACK/DAT_CALLBACK2 (a program's callback receives the
  source's events instead of DAT_EVENT), DF_DSM2 for a DF_APP2 program, and
  a TWAIN 2 source is given the manager's entry points before it opens
  (sane.ds and gphoto2.ds looked for twain_32 only; they now also find
  twaindsm). The program's window from MSG_OPENDSM is read through the
  pointer TWAIN passes (it was the pointer itself).

Gate test/twainscan-gate.sh (UI and TWAIN 2 runs).

